        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>You can do all three things, so yes you can play a card, then use a power (even a power shown on the card you just played).</p><p>Only one card may be played and one power may be used unless you&#39;ve got an ability in play that let&#39;s you do more.&nbsp;</p><p>Yes, if you haven&#39;t done the other two steps (play a card, use a power), then you can draw two cards. This can happen if you&#39;ve chosen not to play/use (maybe because you&#39;ve got nothing good you want to do) or if some other effect has stopped you from plaing/using.&nbsp;</p>",
